' ============================================================
' COMPOSITION AND CONFIGURATION  (bootstrap, outside the layers)
' ============================================================
package "Composition (bootstrap)" #FFFDE7 {
   class AppConfiguration <<dto>> {
     - profile : String
     - httpPort : int
     - libraryPath : Path
     - databasePath : Path
     - databaseUrl : Optional<URI>
     - oidcIssuer : Optional<URI>
     - ffmpegPath : Path
     - exifToolPath : Path
     - cacheEnabled : boolean
     - identityFailureThreshold : int
     - tokenLifetime : Duration
   }
   class ConfigurationLoader <<configuration>> {
     + load(args : List<String>) : AppConfiguration
   }
   abstract class InfrastructureFactory <<abstract factory>> {
     + {abstract} createCatalogRepository() : ICatalogRepository
     + {abstract} createSessionRepository() : ISessionRepository
     + {abstract} createUserRepository() : IUserRepository
     + {abstract} createSharedLinkRepository() : ISharedLinkRepository
     + {abstract} createChangeLog() : IChangeLog
     + {abstract} createOutboxRepository() : IOutboxRepository
     + {abstract} createUnitOfWork() : IUnitOfWork
     + {abstract} createAuditLog() : IAuditLog
     + {abstract} createDataBackup() : IDataBackup
     + {abstract} createConfigurationRepository() : IConfigurationRepository
     + {abstract} createTokenRepository() : ITokenRepository
     + {abstract} createStorage() : IFileStorage
     + {abstract} createIdentityProviders() : List<IIdentityProvider>
     + {abstract} createCredentialRegistry() : ICredentialRegistry
     + {abstract} createMetadataExtractor() : IMetadataExtractor
     + {abstract} createTranscoder() : ITranscoder
     + {abstract} createEventBus() : IEventBus
   }
   class LocalFactory <<concrete factory>>
   class ServerFactory <<concrete factory>>
   class CompositionRoot <<composition root>> {
     - config : AppConfiguration
     - factory : InfrastructureFactory
     + start() : void
     + stop() : void
     - selectFactory(config : AppConfiguration) : InfrastructureFactory
     - decoratePorts() : void
     - auditDrivingPorts() : void
     - buildIngestionChain() : IngestionStep
     - createServices() : void
     - createHttpServer() : Javalin
     - createPrimaryAdapters() : void
     - registerObservers() : void
   }
   InfrastructureFactory <|-- LocalFactory
   InfrastructureFactory <|-- ServerFactory
   CompositionRoot --> AppConfiguration
   ConfigurationLoader ..> AppConfiguration : reads from omnistream.properties and the environment
   CompositionRoot --> InfrastructureFactory : selects by profile
   CompositionRoot ..> IEventSubscriber : registers observers
   CompositionRoot ..> SyncObserver : creates and subscribes

   LocalFactory ..> SqlitePersistenceAdapter : creates
   LocalFactory ..> LocalFileStorageAdapter : creates
   LocalFactory ..> LocalIdentityAdapter : creates
   LocalFactory ..> MetadataAdapter : creates
   LocalFactory ..> TranscodingAdapter : creates
   LocalFactory ..> InMemoryTokenAdapter : creates
   LocalFactory ..> EventBusAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> PostgreSqlPersistenceAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> NetworkFileStorageAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> LocalIdentityAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> OidcIdentityAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> MetadataAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> TranscodingAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> InMemoryTokenAdapter : creates
   ServerFactory ..> EventBusAdapter : creates
 }

' ============================================================
' NOTES
' ============================================================
 note bottom of ICatalogManagement
   Driving ports belong to the domain.
   The domain services implement them and the
   primary adapters invoke them.
 end note

 note bottom of ICatalogRepository
   Driven ports are defined by the domain and
   implemented by the secondary adapters.
   An installation has a single catalog, so
   getCatalog() takes no identifier.
   Queries return snapshots (read only);
   getCatalog() returns the aggregate to change it.
   save() compares the version (optimistic locking) and
   throws VersionConflict if someone else saved it first.
 end note

 note right of IOutboxRepository
   Transactional Outbox:
   CatalogIndex records its events and the persistence
   adapter, inside save(), writes the aggregate and its
   pending events in the same transaction. Nothing else
   writes to the outbox.
   SyncTask invokes EventDispatchService, which
   reads the pending ones, publishes them on the bus and marks them.
   Delivery is at least once: IChangeLog.register
   ignores an EventId it already recorded.
 end note

 note bottom of IUnitOfWork
   Used when an operation touches two aggregates:
   creating a user (User + local credential) and sharing
   a collection (guest User + SharedLink); and by the
   audit decorators, so a change and its AuditEntry are
   saved together. A nested call joins the running one.
 end note

 note bottom of IEventBus
   The bus is the only owner of the observer list.
   The composition root registers SyncObserver once
   at startup. Services keep no lists of their own
   and implement no subscribe()/notify().
 end note

 note bottom of IIdentityProvider
   Strategy: AccessService walks the list and uses the first
   provider that supports the credentials. Local and OIDC
   return the same LinkedIdentity (issuer, subject) and
   the user is resolved with findByIdentity().
   OIDC is wrapped in ResilientIdentityProvider.
 end note

 note bottom of JdbcPersistenceAdapter
   Implements the 10 persistence ports only once,
   with plain JDBC (ADR 0015). SQLite and PostgreSQL only
   change the connection and how the database is dumped
   for backups (Template Method).
   The adapter writes the SQL and assembles each aggregate: it runs
   one query per table, converts the rows with the
   mappers and returns fromSnapshot(...). The change log
   stores events and reuses EventMapper.
   In 2.0 it also implements IRuleRepository, with
   CriterionMapper; the factory provides it like the
   other persistence ports.
 end note

 note bottom of MediaFileMapper
   Row mappers: one per snapshot or value, with no
   state and no SQL. toSnapshot()/toValue() read the current
   row; bind() fills in the parameters of the INSERT or
   UPDATE. They are instances the adapter holds as
   attributes, not static methods.
 end note

 note bottom of ServerFactory
   In version 1.0 only the database changes
   (PostgreSQL): it uses LocalFileStorageAdapter and
   local identity until the network and OIDC
   adapters exist (ADR 0009).
 end note

 note bottom of SyncTask
   Server side of the "Sync changes" use case:
   publishes the pending events so that IChangeLog
   is up to date. Clients read the delta through ISync.
 end note

 note bottom of EventDispatchService
   Domain service invoked by SyncTask.
   It is not a secondary adapter: it coordinates the
   IOutboxRepository and IEventPublisher ports.
 end note

 note bottom of AuthorizedService
   Base class of every service except
   EventDispatchService (see services diagram).
 end note

@enduml
